1) ECR (Only Selected Teams can access ECR, these team are separated allowing them to only push and replace/upgrade only their own images)
2) EKS (Only Selected Teams can access EKS, these team can run/rollout their own pods using their own images in ECR, they can access their own Kubernetes Secrets and ConfigMaps, only in their own namespace pods. Although there's one ConfigMap that can be accessed by only selected Teams)
3) MLFlow running in EKS (Only Selected Teams can access MLFlow, but each of these team has their own workspace for access separation)
4) MWAA/Airflow (Only Selected Teams can access MWAA, but each of these team are separated based on S3 dag access e.g. s3:::dags/team_a/*)
5) POSTGRESQL (Only Selected Teams can access POSTGRESQL, these team have their own schema connected to their login credentials)
6) S3 (Only Selected Teams can access S3, each team can only access their own bucket. Although theres one bucket that only selected teams can access but are still only able to access specific path in that bucket is team based e.g. airflow/connections/team_a and airflow/variables/team_a)

